hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3014","Narrated to us Salm ibn Junādah, narrated to us Wakīʿ, from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿĀʾishah (RA) who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) left my presence while he was at ease and in good spirits. Then he returned to me while he was grieving. So I said, \O Messenger of Allāh"," you left me while you were in such-and-such a state.\"" He said"," \""I entered the Kaʿbah"," and I wish I had not done so. Indeed"," I fear that I may have burdened my nation after me.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
